-- Migration: Store the LUZZI section headings in title1/title2/title3
--
-- luzzi.txt (see 015) carries the headings that precede a verse before a
-- `^`; the 2015 import discarded them, so every LUZZI title column was
-- empty. Each <br />-separated part is a level, outermost first: e.g.
-- 1 Kgs 1:1 -> title1 "REGNO DI SALOMONE (Cap. 1 a 11)", title2 "Vecchiaia
-- di Davide. ...". A parenthetical (chapter range / synoptic parallels) is
-- joined to the heading it follows. 1,639 of the 1,651 headings are a single
-- level and land in title1.
--
-- Four headings fall mid-verse (2 Kgs 25:21, Neh 7:73, John 12:36,
-- Acts 9:19); as titles are per verse, they are stored on that verse.
--
-- Requires 017 (title columns VARCHAR(255)). Generated by
-- scripts/repair_luzzi_from_source.py --emit titles. Idempotent: only
-- writes rows whose three title columns are still empty.

